    "title": "Police searching for Flemington man with dementia - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By NCPA Staff ,\n12 hours ago\nFlemington, Pa. — Police have issued a request for a the public to be on the lookout for a missing Clinton County man.\nState police are searching for George Schiele, a 71-year-old man with dementia who was last seen in the area of 761 Sturdevant St., Flemington.\nSchiele was last seen at about 10:46 p.m. on Aug. 4. Police say he was wearing a gray long-sleeve hoodie, blue jeans, and a red hat.\nDue to his medical condition, he may be confused, disoriented, and unable to find his way home. Residents in the surrounding area are asked to check garages, sheds, outbuildings, porches, and other locations where Schiele may have sought shelter overnight.\nAnyone with information is asked to contact police immediately by calling 911 or the Pennsylvania State Police's Lamar station at 570-726-6000.\n3",
    "summary": "Flemington, Pa. — Police have issued a request for a the public to be on the lookout for a missing Clinton County man. State police are searching for George Schiele, a 71-year-old man with dementia who was last seen in the area of 761 Sturdevant St., Flemington. Police say he was wearing a gray long-sleeve hoodie, blue jeans, and a red hat. Due to his medical condition, he may be confused, disoriented, and unable to find his way home.",
